three-dimensional space and of four-dimensional Euclidean space; of the \
Lorentz group of $2+1$ dimensions, equal to $\\\\mathfrak{sl}(2,\\\\mathbb \
R)$; $\\\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$ the simple Lie algebra of dimension 3 over any \
field; $\\\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ isospin; $\\\\mathfrak{spin}(7)$ of dimension \
21; the exceptional Lie algebra $\\\\mathfrak g_2$ (compact, dimension 14) \
and its complex form (real dimension 28)\>\""}], ",", " ", 
